# builtin-is-contractive
--- uses: ["core"]
# return type is Bool: both true and false branches return Bool.
# This pins the return type contract — the builtin always returns a Bool value,
# not a Variant or other type, regardless of whether the input is contractive.
#
# Two calls: one on a plain Int (contractive → Bool(true)), one on a
# TypeNode.RecursiveRef (non-contractive → Bool(false)).
# The `and` of the first with `[not false]` of the second gives Bool(true).
[
  leaf-node: 42
  ref-node:  [builtin-variant "TypeNode.RecursiveRef" [name: "x"]]
  leaf-ok:   [builtin-is-contractive leaf-node]
  ref-ok:    [not [builtin-is-contractive ref-node]]
  both:      [and leaf-ok ref-ok]
]
both
=== out
Bool(true)
